  "findings": [
    {
      "finding": "C++ public API is not the Python wrapper API",
      "evidence": "dbObject.h line165 declares uint32_t getId() const. dbObject.cpp lines21-23 implements it via internal getImpl()->getOID(). Neither declaration establishes a Python getOID method."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Pinned Python interface does not parse the base declaration",
      "evidence": "src/odb/src/swig/python/CMakeLists.txt selects ../common/odb.i. Its %include list parses db.h but not dbObject.h; the C++ #include is compilation-only. All common/python .i sources inspected have no getId/getOID declaration or rename/extension. swig_lib.cmake uses this interface, with no includeall or base-class injection in its options."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Failure risk covers every newly used inherited getId call",
      "evidence": "Current ownership uses getId on technology layers, nets, wires, ITerms, BTerms, BPins, SWires, SBoxes, fills, obstructions, instances and boxes. Only dbTechLayer failure is reported actual; other types remain a source-derived exposure risk. Pure raw projection source has no getId. No rule.getId currently exists."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Layer number and routing level are not raw OIDs",
      "evidence": "db.h9408 documents getNumber as mask-order;9420 routing level. dbTechLayer.cpp2213 returns number_,2219 returns rlevel_, whereas2302 getTechLayer(tech,dbid) uses layer_tbl_->getPtr(dbid). Do not substitute either ordinal for a raw wire layer operand."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Static typed lookup can preserve known raw operands without inventing a public base accessor",
      "evidence": "db.h explicitly declares getTechLayer(tech,oid), getTechLayerRule(tech/block,oid), getVia(block,oid), getTechVia(tech,oid), and typed object lookups. dbWireCodec.cpp stores the native internal OID for PATH/SHORT/VWIRE, VIA/TECHVIA and ITerm/BTerm operands. Any replacement must retain raw operand bytes/indices and validate the actual object returned; source inspection does not qualify a replacement implementation or runtime API."
    }
  ],
